farmland-atlas/kansas/wallace-county"],["ARC or PLC in Wallace County","/arc-plc/kansas/wallace-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and February to March came in under 90% of normal in 42 of those 75 years. In 2025, August to September hit 159% of normal on the middle of the grids, while January to February sat at 67%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 14% of normal on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
